[6.975,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your AWS account (region eu-south-2); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. SSH key: import the stack's own key pair into the region (.openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-el-a102129-key.pem)\r\n  2. Template: render the elastic template into .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-pro-elastic.yaml\r\n     and its parameters into .openvidu/aws/cfn-parameters.json (0600)\r\n  3. Bucket: stage the template in the S3 bucket openvidu-cfn-templates-***-eu-south-2 (created once, reused by every stack)\r\n  4. Network: the region's default VPC, vpc-0e2358cb016b9fef5, and its default subnets: subnet-0497cd2d92bbfd794 (eu-south-2a), subnet-02776aa519c2198f1 (eu-south-2b), subnet-0053e4f7269e42ebc (eu-south-2c)\r\n     the master in subnet-0497cd2d92bbfd794 (eu-south-2a); the media nodes in all of them\r\n  5. Machines: Create the CloudFormation stack openvidu-e2e-aws-el-a102129 with the master and the media nodes: the master installs OpenVidu and the media nodes join it (about 7 minutes)\r\n  6. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on AWS…\r\n   · SSH key pair for this stack: .openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-el-a102129-key.pem\r\n"]
